-+# Codex Patch Handoff — MTGA Collection Reader / WB Fox Bridge 5.1.0
-+
-+## 1. Decision record
-+
-+The collection architecture is now locked:
-+
-+```text
-+MTGA read-only process memory  → primary ownership authority
-+Arena local card database      → Arena ID identity authority
-+Scryfall                       → optional enrichment outside this patch
-+Manual JSON snapshot           → permanent ownership fallback
-+Player.log                     → supplemental activity/trigger only
-+Screenshot OCR                 → calibration only, never collection authority
-+```
-+
-+Do not reintroduce Player.log or full-screen OCR as the canonical collection source.
-+
-+## 2. User requirements carried forward
-+
-+- Windows desktop companion.
-+- Simple GUI.
-+- Complete owned collection represented as Arena ID plus quantity.
-+- Prefer no manual anchors.
-+- Automatically derive anchors from Collection screenshots when possible.
-+- Manual exact-card/quantity anchors are acceptable as a fallback.
-+- Player.log remains useful, but only as activity input or a trigger for a fresh memory scan.
-+- Empty, partial, or incompatible scans must never overwrite the last valid collection.
-+- Every accepted snapshot must be retained.
-+- Unknown Arena IDs must be retained.
-+- Local WB Fox service must bind only to loopback and require authentication.
-+
-+## 3. Patch contents
-+
-+### New files
-+
-+```text
-+provider_contract.py
-+memory_provider.py
-+calibration.py
-+manual_import.py
-+bridge_service.py
-+run_bridge.bat
-+PATCH_NOTES_v5.1.0.md
-+CODEX_PATCH_HANDOFF.md
-+```
-+
-+### Replaced or materially changed
-+
-+```text
-+mtg.py
-+collection_store.py
-+README.md
-+CHANGES.md
-+VALIDATION.md
-+app_manifest.json
-+installed_version.txt
-+install.bat
-+run_reader.bat
-+card_database.py
-+```
-+
-+### Retained for calibration/compatibility
-+
-+```text
-+visual_scan.py
-+player_log.py
-+exports.py
-+patch_old_install.ps1
-+patch_old_install.bat
-+```
-+
-+`player_log.py` may remain as an isolated parser for future activity features, but no GUI ownership workflow may call it to merge the total collection.
-+
-+## 4. Provider contract
-+
-+The canonical Python contract is in `provider_contract.py`.
-+
-+Equivalent TypeScript contract for WB Fox:
-+
-+```ts
-+interface CollectionProvider {
-+  detect(): Promise<ProviderStatus>;
-+  readCollection(): Promise<CollectionSnapshot>;
-+}
-+
-+interface CollectionSnapshot {
-+  schemaVersion: 1;
-+  snapshotId: string;
-+  source: "mtga-memory" | "manual-import";
-+  mtgaClientVersion: string | null;
-+  capturedAt: string;
-+  cards: Array<{
-+    arenaId: number;
-+    quantity: number;
-+  }>;
-+  diagnostics: Record<string, unknown>;
-+}
-+```
-+
-+Required providers:
-+
-+```text
-+MtgaMemoryProvider        Primary
-+ManualJsonImportProvider  Permanent fallback
-+PlayerLogActivityProvider Supplemental only; never returns authoritative ownership
-+```
-+
-+## 5. Current memory implementation
-+
-+`memory_provider.py`:
-+
-+1. Finds `MTGA.exe` with the Windows Tool Help process snapshot API.
-+2. Opens the process with only:
-+
-+```text
-+PROCESS_VM_READ
-+PROCESS_QUERY_INFORMATION
-+```
-+
-+3. Does not request `PROCESS_VM_WRITE`, `PROCESS_VM_OPERATION`, thread access, token access, injection, or debugging privileges.
-+4. Resolves screenshot/manual anchors into possible Arena printing IDs.
-+5. Searches readable committed pages for the packed little-endian pair:
-+
-+```text
-+uint32 arenaId
-+uint32 quantity
-+```
-+
-+6. Reads a bounded region around matches.
-+7. Detects plausible alternating ID/quantity blocks.
-+8. Requires:
-+   - at least one exact anchor quantity hit;
-+   - substantial Arena database coverage;
-+   - a minimum number of known Arena IDs;
-+   - plausible ownership quantities.
-+9. Produces a complete `CollectionSnapshot` only after validation.
-+10. Fails closed if no candidate satisfies validation.
-+
-+### Important limitation
-+
-+This is a hardened anchor-pattern provider, not yet a direct managed-object traversal provider. The next recommended implementation is a versioned MTGA managed-memory adapter that reads the live inventory dictionary directly. Keep it behind the same `CollectionProvider` contract.
-+
-+## 6. Screenshot calibration
-+
-+`calibration.py` uses the existing capture and OCR components for one purpose only: generate anchors.
-+
-+Flow:
-+
-+```text
-+Capture short stable-frame burst
-+→ detect Collection card rectangles
-+→ read visible quantity diamonds
-+→ OCR visible card titles
-+→ reject uncertain/unowned records
-+→ prefer names with fewer Arena printings
-+→ return up to five anchor name/quantity pairs
-+```
-+
-+Rules:
-+
-+- Never merge screenshot OCR results into the saved collection.
-+- Never claim the screenshot is a complete collection.
-+- Save the latest calibration screenshot for diagnostics.
-+- When calibration fails, use manual anchors or manual JSON import.
-+- Do not silently invent quantities or names.
-+
-+## 7. Manual anchor fallback
-+
-+The GUI exposes three optional anchor rows.
-+
-+Each requires:
-+
-+```text
-+exact or confidently corrected card name
-+owned quantity 1–4
-+```
-+
-+Multiple anchors reduce false positives. Codex may expand the UI to five anchors, but must not require all fields.
-+
-+## 8. Snapshot persistence
-+
-+`collection_store.py` adds `collection_snapshots`.
-+
-+Each accepted snapshot retains:
-+
-+```text
-+snapshot_id
-+scan_id
-+schema_version
-+source
-+mtga_client_version
-+captured_at
-+stored_at
-+unique_cards
-+total_copies
-+payload_json
-+diagnostics_json
-+```
-+
-+`apply_authoritative_snapshot` is the only approved full replacement path.
-+
-+### Required behavior
-+
-+- Reject empty snapshots.
-+- Preserve unknown Arena IDs as review rows.
-+- Compare against the last saved collection.
-+- Require user confirmation when unique IDs or total copies fall below 65% of the saved collection.
-+- Store the accepted snapshot before replacing live rows.
-+- Use deterministic snapshot IDs.
-+- Reapplying the same snapshot must be idempotent.
-+- Never delete snapshot history during a normal sync.
-+
-+### Follow-up work
-+
-+Add a user-visible rollback button that restores an earlier retained snapshot through a new audited scan session. Do not mutate snapshot history itself.
-+
-+## 9. Manual JSON import
-+
-+`manual_import.py` accepts:
-+
-+1. Canonical snapshot object with `cards`.
-+2. Raw card-record list.
-+3. Numeric Arena-ID/quantity map.
-+
-+Supported aliases:
-+
-+```text
-+arenaId | arena_id | grpId | id
-+quantity | owned | count | qty
-+```
-+
-+Rules:
-+
-+- Arena ID must be a positive integer.
-+- Quantity must be positive and no greater than 255.
-+- Quantities above four are retained but surfaced in validation diagnostics.
-+- Duplicate IDs merge by maximum quantity.
-+- Empty result is rejected.
-+
-+Do not loosen validation to silently ignore malformed records.
-+
-+## 10. Player.log boundary
-+
-+The GUI action **Check Player.log and sync memory** does only this:
-+
-+1. Resolve a current log file.
-+2. Record that activity input exists.
-+3. Start the memory provider.
-+
-+It must not parse deck arrays, account inventory, or incidental card notifications into total ownership.
-+
-+Future `PlayerLogActivityProvider` output may include:
-+
-+```text
-+played decks
-+match history
-+rank events
-+draft events
-+wildcards/currency
-+newly acquired-card events
-+rescan triggers
-+```
-+
-+These events must remain separate from `CollectionSnapshot`.
-+
-+## 11. Local bridge API
-+
-+`bridge_service.py` provides:
-+
-+```text
-+GET  /v1/status
-+GET  /v1/collection
-+POST /v1/shutdown
-+```
-+
-+Current security:
-+
-+- loopback binding only;
-+- local-client check;
-+- per-install bearer token;
-+- no CORS wildcard;
-+- no Player.log endpoint;
-+- no process-memory endpoint;
-+- only latest accepted snapshot is returned.
-+
-+Required request header:
-+
-+```text
-+Authorization: Bearer <Data\bridge_token.txt>
-+```
-+
-+### Release hardening still required
-+
-+- Apply a Windows ACL so only the installing user and administrators can read `bridge_token.txt`.
-+- Rotate the token during reinstall only with explicit migration behavior.
-+- Add structured access logs without card payloads or tokens.
-+- Add rate limiting appropriate for localhost.
-+- Ensure the server cannot bind to a non-loopback address through configuration or malformed CLI input.
-+- Add a stable WB Fox pairing UI so the user explicitly approves data sharing.
-+- Display the exact fields sent to WB Fox before first sync.
-+
-+## 12. Licensing boundary
-+
-+The open-source `mtga-tracker-daemon` repository is a useful architecture reference and demonstrates managed-memory collection access, `/cards`, and local card-database resolution. Its repository license is GPL-3.0.
-+
-+Do not copy GPL implementation code into a proprietary WB Fox binary without an explicit licensing decision. Acceptable options require legal/product approval, for example:
-+
-+- independently implement the behavior from clean-room requirements;
-+- ship a clearly separate GPL companion with complete corresponding source and required notices;
-+- obtain a different license from the copyright holder.
-+
-+The current 5.1.0 patch is an independent Python implementation of the required behavior and does not vendor that repository.
-+
-+## 13. Update resilience
-+
-+Codex must preserve these boundaries:
-+
-+```text
-+provider_contract.py      stable public contract
-+memory_provider.py        replaceable MTGA adapter
-+calibration.py            replaceable calibration adapter
-+manual_import.py          permanent fallback
-+collection_store.py       snapshot safety and history
-+bridge_service.py         localhost transport only
-+```
-+
-+Recommended next adapter structure:
-+
-+```text
-+providers/
-+  contract.py
-+  mtga_memory/
-+    provider.py
-+    process_reader.py
-+    client_version.py
-+    layouts/
-+      2026_61_30.py
-+    fixtures/
-+      2026_61_30/
-+  manual_json.py
-+  player_log_activity.py
-+```
-+
-+Unknown MTGA versions must return:
-+
-+```text
-+Collection sync temporarily incompatible with this MTGA update.
-+Your last valid collection is unchanged.
-+Use manual JSON import or manual calibration while support is updated.
-+```
-+
-+Never fall back to weak heuristics and return plausible-looking incorrect data.
-+
-+## 14. Compatibility fixtures
-+
-+For every supported MTGA client version, retain sanitized fixtures that do not contain account credentials or personal identifiers:
-+
-+```text
-+client version
-+module metadata
-+layout/field names or offsets
-+representative collection block bytes
-+expected Arena ID/quantity pairs
-+negative/random memory samples
-+screenshot calibration samples at supported resolutions/scales
-+```
-+
-+Tests must prove:
-+
-+- correct version selects correct adapter;
-+- unknown version fails closed;
-+- random memory does not pass validation;
-+- one anchor collision does not validate the wrong block;
-+- multiple anchors select the correct block;
-+- unknown Arena IDs survive normalization;
-+- quantities are not truncated without diagnostics.
-+
-+## 15. Acceptance criteria
-+
-+### Memory provider
-+
-+- [ ] Detects running `MTGA.exe`.
