-+# Patch Notes — 5.1.0
-+
-+## Corrected architecture
-+
-+- Removed `Player.log` as a collection ownership provider.
-+- Made read-only MTGA process memory the primary collection source.
-+- Changed visual OCR from full collection extraction to screenshot-assisted memory calibration.
-+- Retained manual card anchors as a fallback.
-+- Added permanent manual JSON snapshot import.
-+- Added complete snapshot retention and suspicious-drop confirmation.
-+- Added an authenticated localhost WB Fox Bridge service.
-+
-+## Security changes
-+
-+- MTGA is opened with `PROCESS_VM_READ | PROCESS_QUERY_INFORMATION` only.
-+- No process write, injection, traffic interception, credential collection, or Arena-token reuse.
-+- Bridge binds to `127.0.0.1` and requires a per-install bearer token.
-+- Bridge returns only the latest accepted collection snapshot.
-+
-+## Removed behavior
-+
-+- Player.log collection payload parsing no longer writes to `collection.db`.
-+- Deferred OCR scrolling is no longer the primary collection path.
-+- A failed or empty scan cannot erase the last valid collection.
-+
-+## Compatibility behavior
-+
-+- Screenshot calibration is attempted first.
-+- Manual exact-name/quantity anchors remain available when calibration fails.
-+- Unknown MTGA layouts fail closed with a compatibility message.
